				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$ \left\{\mathrm{total}\kern0.5em \mathrm{reads}\kern0.5em \times \kern0.5em \left(\frac{\mathrm{paternal}\kern0.5em \mathrm{reads}}{\mathrm{maternnal}\kern0.5em \mathrm{reads}\kern0.5em +\kern0.5em \mathrm{paternal}\kern0.5em \mathrm{reads}}\right)\right\} $$\end{document}totalreads×paternalreadsmaternnalreads+paternalreads. Differential expression analysis for the paternal-X expression level was then carried out using DESeq2.
